Server errors:


- The submit function and action property we saw earlier have another interesting feature: 🔥if the
    action you provide returns errors, they are automatically added to the errors() of the
    corresponding fields (or to the form if you don’t provide a field).
    register.ts:

        protected readonly loginForm = form(this.credentials, {
            submission: {
                action: async () => {
                    const { login, password } = this.credentials();
                    try {
                        await this.userService.authenticate(login, password);
                        await this.router.navigateByUrl('/');
                        return;
                    } catch (error) {
                        //👇 add an error to the form
                        const message = (error as Error).message;
                        return [{ kind: 'invalid-credentials', message }];
                    }
                }
            }
        })
    
    This allows merging errors detected client-side with errors detected server-side.